---
term: Highest human charter
section: structure
order: 70
definition: The largest charter that people create, which answers only to the [[Natural Charter]].
seeAlso:
  - nested-corporation
  - natural-charter
  - ecumenical-charter
  - independent-formation
---
Authority has to stop somewhere. The Social Charter places the highest human charter above national and other high-level charters and below the constraints of reality.

The highest human charter isn't the only charter without a parent. Any charter can exist ex natura, directly under the Natural Charter, through [[independent formation]]. The highest human charter is the largest of them: the largest coalition that shares a real interest.

```diagram
Natural Charter
  ├ Highest human charter
  │   ▼ National and other high-level charters
  │   ▼ Subordinate charters
  │   ▼ Individuals
  └ Other charters ex natura
```

The position doesn't require any particular design. Any [[ecumenical charter]] that the coalition adopts can fill it.
